Q: HTML table rules till the size of border
A: <p>You'll want to make the last row expand the height of the table with empty space. In this way the rules will continue to the bottom.</p>
<p>Place an empty, tall div in one of your columns of the last row. 1 pixels wide is fine, but any width (including 0) less than the width of your actual content in that column is ideal. Otherwise the column will get wider.</p>
<p>Set the height to an arbitrarily large value. This only works because your parent div has overflow hidden. If you didnt have that there then you would need to use javascript to dynamically calculate the needed height of the row stretching div.</p>
