   If your classes are placed in the `generated` directory, make sure Dagger is configured to load classes from there. This can typically be done by adding the `META-INF/services` directory to the classpath.

   ```sh
   -Pdagger2.moduleClasspath=<path_to_generated_directory>
   ```

   In your `build.gradle` or `settings.gradle` file, you can add the following line:
   ```groovy
   task copyDaggerModuleFiles(type: Copy) {
       from <path_to_generated_directory>
       into <path_to_generated_directory>
   }

