Q: Asynchronous Request Chaining
A: <p>Asynchronous loops are a pain in the ass. As a rule of thumb, if you want to do them by hand you need to rewrite the for loop as a recursive function.</p>

<pre><code>function sequence_synchronous(steps){
  for(var i=0; i&lt;steps.length; i++){
    steps[i]();
  }
  return;
}


function sequence_async(steps, callback){
  var i = 0;
  var next_step = function(){
    if(i &gt;= steps.length){
       callback();
    }else{
       steps[i](function(){
          i++;
          next_step();
       });
    }
  }
  next_step();
}
</code></pre>

<p>Note that this doesn't attempt to build a big chain of callbacks before calling the first one - all we did was convert the traditional for loop into continuation passing style.</p>

<p>I would highly recommend looking for a library to do this for you though.</p>

